sched/fair: per-LLC idle bitmap v2 (lazy clear, wrap from target)

Rework of the per-LLC idle_cpus hint on sched_domain_shared.

v1 wrote the shared bitmap unconditionally on every idle enter and
exit, and walked set bits from a fixed (target+1) start. Measured
wakeup-storm busy-phase regressions vs stock 7.2.9 pointed at those
two behaviors (shared-line bouncing across the LLC, and pile-up onto
low-numbered CPUs).

v2 changes:

1. Cut shared writes.
   - llc_idle_enter() only sets the bit when it was clear
     (test_bit before set_bit).
   - Idle exit no longer clears: put_prev_task_idle does not touch the
     bitmap. A waker that finds a candidate busy clears the stale bit
     (also test-before-clear). Hotplug still clears via llc_idle_clear()
     after set_cpu_active(false), so a deactivated CPU cannot re-publish.
   - Domain-attach seeding is likewise test-first.

2. Search from the target.
   - Snap LLC span & p->cpus_ptr & idle_cpus into the select_rq_mask
     scratch, then for_each_cpu_wrap(..., target) so candidates near
     the waker/wakee are preferred. Cluster-first preference is kept
     (same shape as the linear walk). Affinity uses p->cpus_ptr exactly
     as the existing walk does.

3. Unchanged: SIS_UTIL early-out, has_idle_core / select_idle_core,
   select_idle_capacity, and the capped linear walk as fallback when
   the bitmap yields nothing.

Applies to stock 7.2.9 with patch -p1.

